WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.907
"Side Effects of Osteoporosis Medications
Like Fosamax, Boniva, and Reclast"

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.360
Potential lack of efficacy
is not the only reason

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.700
why most people prescribed
bisphosphonate drugs

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.420
for osteoporosis like Fosamax,
Actonel, Boniva, or Reclast,

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.640
may stop taking them
within a year.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.060
There are two rare
but devastating side effects:

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.840
osteonecrosis of the jaw
and atypical femur fractures,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.300
that contributed to around
a 50 percent drop

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.740
in the use
of this class of drugs

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.580
when they came to light.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.860
The New York Times article
noting the decline

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.240
explained the reasoning:

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.840
"Reports of the drugs
causing jawbones to rot

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.180
and thighbones
to snap in two

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.760
have shaken many
osteoporosis patients so much,

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:45.900
that they say
they would rather

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.000
take their chances
with the disease."

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.180
The jaw-rot syndrome
that prevents many

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.880
from initiating treatment for
fear of "their jaw falling off"

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.300
can severely impact many aspects
of quality of life,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.460
but is exceedingly rare,

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.100
affecting at most
one in a thousand patients

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.600
treated for osteoporosis.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.080
Atypical femur fractures can
occur more frequently, though,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.440
as many as one in 300 users
treated for three years.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.480
They are called "atypical,"

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.820
because they occur
not after a fall or trauma,

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.100
but just during
routine activities,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.960
like walking,
twisting at the waist,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.820
or even just standing still.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.060
Your femur,
your thigh bone,

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.900
the biggest bone in your body,
just breaks in half.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.840
Too cruel an irony from a drug

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.420
that's supposed to protect
your bones.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.790
This is what it looks like
on x-ray.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.150
Ouch.

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:40.560
Bisphosphonates work
by inhibiting the action

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.440
of a type of bone cell
called osteoclasts.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.380
Your entire skeleton
is constantly being remodeled

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:49.020
with bone added in some spots
and taken away in others

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.000
to conform
to changing demands.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.820
The cells that are continually
laying down new bone

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.140
are called osteoblasts,

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.940
and the ones
that chisel away old bone

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.500
are called the osteoclasts.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.520
It makes sense, then,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.340
that curbing the 'clasts
could prevent bone loss.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:05.700
But by reducing
the active remodeling process,

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.520
bisphosphonates can "freeze"
the skeleton,

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.120
allowing for the accumulation
of microcracks over time,

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.160
resulting in stress fractures.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.540
Other osteoporosis drugs like
denosumab, sold, as "Prolia,"

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.620
prevent the same formation of
osteoclasts in the first place

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.540
and have been plagued
by the same kinds

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.940
of rare but disturbing
side effects.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.620
As with anything in life,

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.680
it all comes down to risks
versus benefits.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.240
How many hip fractures
are prevented

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.920
for every femur that snaps?

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.720
It depends on your race

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.460
and how long
you're on these drugs.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.200
After five years,
in white women,

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.420
36 hip fractures
are prevented

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.520
for every
atypical femur fracture.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.420
Hispanic women only get half
the benefit, about 18 to 1.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.860
And for Asian women,

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.200
it's only about
5 hip fractures prevented

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.240
for every femur fracture caused.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.820
The study claims it failed
to accrue enough data

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:57.480
on Black women.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.740
At ten years of drug exposure,
the ratios get worse,

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.100
16:1 for white women,
5:1 for Hispanic women,

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.680
and only 1.5:1 for Asian women,

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.780
meaning that
the devastating fractures

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:12.720
prevented and caused
in Asian women

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.280
are nearly comparable.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.820
A nationwide survey
of resident physicians

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.220
found that knowledge regarding
osteoporosis diagnosis

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.480
and treatment was poor,

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.120
with a particularly striking
lack of knowledge

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.700
regarding the two
serious drug side effects.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.420
The good news is that
after stopping the drugs,

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.980
the risk of femur fracture

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.040
rapidly drops by 70 percent
within a year,

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.800
leading to the suggestion
that a drug "holiday"

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.600
be considered
after a few years

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.180
on the drug to help mediate
the risk.

